message: "If you use this software or its documentation, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Energy-Optimal Retrieval Depth in Retrieval-Augmented Generation"
abstract: >-
  A research harness and decision-theoretic study of retrieval depth in
  retrieval-augmented generation. The project measures joules per correct answer
  E(k) = E[J_k] / E[C_k] under a pre-registered accuracy gate, tests an
  optimal-depth elasticity identity, estimates a price-of-static-depth bound, and
  evaluates a certification-cost threshold for deciding whether calibration is
  worth its energy. The initial pilot is MARGINAL: a static 2 percentage-point
  claim failed at the boundary, while a 5 percentage-point non-inferiority
  policy at k = 4 saved 69.3% of energy in the pilot. No confirmatory results are
  claimed in version 0.1.0.
